/*---
compatibilityVersion: naiscript-1.0
id: 6d0e7c1b-2a54-4f0e-9b7d-3c5a8e21f4a9
name: Scenario Probe
version: 0.3.0
description: How often does a Build turn keep a thing to come out of everything the story model is shown, and how much does it build that nobody asked for?
memoryLimit: 8
---*/

// These four constants are copies of the shipped Build prompt, its Gritty
// register, the fixed Build instruction and the Build prefill in
// src/core/utils/prompts.ts;
// tests/tools/scenario-probe.test.ts fails if they drift.
const SCENARIO_BUILD_PROMPT = "You are the Scenario Engine's builder. A writer and a collaborator have been talking about a story. You record what they settled on as the conditions the story can grow from: pressures, the people and places under them, and how things stand between them. You never record a plot, an arc, a goal or an ending. Another model will continue this story from a blank page, and it acts on whatever it is shown: told that something will happen, it writes it happening at once, or as already done. So everything you record says only what is so when the story opens.\n\nThe context block above the conversation lists everything that exists under [WORLD], and how things stand under [THREADS]. A list that is missing is empty. The writer's last message says what to build.\n\nThink out loud first, in plain sentences, answering in order:\n1. What did the writer say? Go through the writer's own messages and name each person, place, pressure and standing between people they stated, each thing they said is hidden or unspoken, and each thing they want to happen.\n2. Does anything the collaborator said disagree with something the writer said: an age, an amount, who does a thing, whether a thing has happened? Name each one. The writer's statement is recorded exactly as the writer gave it and the collaborator's is dropped. Only the writer changes what the writer said, and silence is not a change.\n3. What else did the collaborator add? A new detail that disagrees with nothing counts as accepted unless the writer turned it down: a person, a place, an object, a fact that is so when the story opens. A scene it narrates is not a fact, in whatever tense it is told: someone arriving, someone finding something, someone learning something. That is for the story to do, and it is left out, however much the writer wants that ending.\n4. Which of those is already under [WORLD] or [THREADS]? Those need no command unless later talk changed them.\n5. Is anything hidden from someone in the story: a thing done that they have not been told, a thing owed, a thing kept back? The whole of it goes in the private segment of a THREAD, the deed as well as the silence about it, and in no summary and no state. The story model writes whatever it is shown as something everyone knows.\n6. For each thing the writer wants, is it already so when the story opens? YES: it is recorded as fact, in a summary or a THREAD's state if it is open knowledge, in a private segment if it is hidden. NO: it is something to come, and it goes in the wish segment of the THREAD whose cast it concerns, and nowhere else: not in that THREAD's title, and not in any name, even when the writer gave the thing to come a name of its own. Where the conversation gave nothing that makes it possible, add nothing: do not invent an object, a place or a circumstance to carry the wish.\n\nThen write the commands, one per line, and stop.\n\nBuild only what the conversation supports. Write nothing the conversation did not raise: no extra people to fill a town, no place nobody mentioned. What the writer stated is never changed to fit something the collaborator said. When something is hidden or unspoken, or the writer named something they want to happen, write a THREAD for it. If there is nothing new to record, say so and write no command.\n\nCOMMANDS:\n[CREATE <TYPE> \"<Name>\" | summary of one to three sentences]\n[REVISE \"<Name>\" | new summary]\n[RENAME \"<Old>\" → \"<New>\"]\n[DELETE \"<Name>\"]\n[THREAD \"<Title>\" | \"<A>\", \"<B>\" | state | private | wish]\n<TYPE> is CHARACTER, LOCATION, FACTION, SYSTEM, SITUATION or TOPIC.\nA SITUATION is a pressure. Its summary reads \"what is happening; what keeps it from settling\", and stops there. The REGISTER note gives the most SITUATIONs the whole scenario may hold, so count the ones under [WORLD] before writing another.\nA THREAD names one to four elements and always has all five segments. Its title is shown to the story model like its state, so it names what stands now: a place, a thing shared, a bond. Never title a THREAD or name an element after something hidden or something to come. state is how things stand now as anyone in the story could say it, and it is shown to the story model. private is what is true now and hidden, owed or unspoken; the story model never sees it. wish is what the writer wants to come about; the story model never sees it. Leave private or wish empty between its bars when there is none. A THREAD whose title is already under [THREADS] rewrites that Thread's state, private and wish: a segment left empty keeps what is stored, and the cast does not change.\nAnything under [WORLD] may be revised or renamed. Only a line marked * may be deleted. What you write is real at once. If [REJECTED LAST TURN] is present, correct each command as its line says; where the line says a thing cannot be done, do not write that command again.\n\nEXAMPLE. The writer said that Hesper Vane is a lock-keeper on a dying canal who alone holds the sluice keys; that her brother Corin has already sold his half of the lock house to the barge company and has not told her; and that they want her to end up flooding the cut to stop them. The collaborator answered that the company's agent, Mr Rudd, lodges at the Bargeman's Rest, that Corin is nineteen and has never worked the lock, and then narrated a scene: Rudd comes up the towpath with a writ, and Hesper reads her brother's name on it. The writer had said Corin worked the lock beside her for ten years, and has not written since. Nothing is built yet.\nThe writer said: Hesper Vane keeps a lock on a dying canal and alone holds the sluice keys; her brother Corin worked it beside her for ten years; he has sold his half of the lock house to the barge company and has not told her; and they want her to flood the cut. The collaborator said Corin is nineteen and never worked the lock, which disagrees with the writer's ten years beside her, so the ten years are recorded and the collaborator's version is dropped. It added Mr Rudd, the company's agent, lodging at the Bargeman's Rest, which disagrees with nothing and is taken; and it narrated Rudd arriving with a writ and Hesper reading Corin's name on it, which is a scene and not a fact, so it is left out: nothing recorded says she has learned of the sale. None of it is under [WORLD]. The sale is hidden from Hesper, so the sale and the silence both go in private and neither summary mentions it. The flooding is to come, so it goes in the wish; her keys are what make it possible, and the writer gave them. The THREAD is titled for the house the two of them share, which is so now, and not for the sale or the flooding.\n[CREATE SITUATION \"The Company's Offer\" | The barge company is buying the lock houses along the cut to close it and take the water for its mills; every keeper who sells makes the next refusal cost more.]\n[CREATE CHARACTER \"Hesper Vane\" | Keeps Tolland Lock as her mother did. Rope-scarred palms, and a ring of sluice keys on her belt that she counts by touch.]\n[CREATE CHARACTER \"Corin Vane\" | Her brother, ten years at the lock beside her. Clean boots on a towpath these days, and a town coat he keeps on indoors.]\n[CREATE CHARACTER \"Mr Rudd\" | The barge company's agent on the cut. Lodges at the Bargeman's Rest and pays for his suppers a week ahead.]\n[CREATE LOCATION \"Tolland Lock House\" | Damp plaster and coal smoke; one kitchen, two names on the deed. The sluice wheel stands in the yard where anyone on the towpath can see who turns it.]\n[THREAD \"Half the House\" | \"Hesper Vane\", \"Corin Vane\" | Hesper Vane and Corin Vane keep Tolland Lock House between them. Hesper Vane holds the only set of sluice keys. | Corin Vane has sold his half of Tolland Lock House to the barge company and been paid. Hesper Vane has not been told. | Hesper Vane floods the cut to stop the company.]";
const REGISTER = "REGISTER, Gritty: Three pressures at most in the whole scenario, with stakes that last. Each sets two things someone values against each other, where walking away is possible and costs something real.";
const SCENARIO_BUILD_INSTRUCTION = "Build what we have discussed.";
const SCENARIO_BUILD_PREFILL = "The writer said:";

// 60 generations against a 2048-token-per-240s output bucket: it takes a while.
// A generation is refused outright when the bucket holds less than max_tokens,
// so every run waits for the bucket first. Read every count with its
// denominator: a run that threw was not measured and is not a failing run.
const RUNS = 20;
const MODEL = "glm-4-6";
// The shipped Build turn asks for 1024 per call and continues; the probe does
// not continue, so a reply cut off at 1024 shows up as a run with no THREAD. A
// generation is refused unless the bucket holds max_tokens.
const PARAMS = { model: MODEL, max_tokens: 1024, temperature: 0.9, min_p: 0.05 };

// Each fixture is a short Plan conversation, written by hand, then an empty
// Build send. A glassworks and an observatory: unlike the prompt's canal, so
// no fixture is a copy of the example the prompt carries.
const TALKS = {
  ToCome: [
    {
      role: "user",
      content:
        "A glassblower's widow, Maud Tarn, runs the furnace house with her late husband's apprentice, Wick. I want it to end in what the town will call the Quillane Fire, when Wick burns the furnace house down.",
    },
    {
      role: "assistant",
      content:
        "Then page one needs what Wick already resents and what he already has his hands on. He banks the furnace alone at night and knows the flues better than Maud does. What does she owe him that she hasn't paid?",
    },
    {
      role: "user",
      content:
        "His indenture ended when her husband died and she never signed his release. She needs him and can't afford a journeyman's wage.",
    },
  ],
  AlreadySo: [
    {
      role: "user",
      content:
        "A glassblower's widow, Maud Tarn, runs the furnace house with her late husband's apprentice, Wick. Two winters ago Wick burned the furnace house down in what the town calls the Quillane Fire, and Maud rebuilt it without a word.",
    },
    {
      role: "assistant",
      content:
        "So the fire is history and the silence is the live thing. Everyone in town knows who set it, and she kept him on anyway. Has she ever asked him why?",
    },
    {
      role: "user",
      content:
        "Never. He still works for her and neither of them has spoken of it.",
    },
  ],
  TwoWishes: [
    {
      role: "user",
      content:
        "Two astronomers share one telescope on a mountain: Ilse Marrow, the younger, and Osric Hale. I want Ilse to end up publishing, under her own name, what she will call the Vessarine Catalogue, and I want Osric to finally leave for the post at Orrowmere.",
    },
    {
      role: "assistant",
      content:
        "Then what matters now is whose name is on the observing log, and why Osric is still on the mountain. Who do the plates belong to tonight?",
    },
    {
      role: "user",
      content:
        "The log is in his name by observatory rule, though she takes most of the plates. Orrowmere has written to him twice and he has not answered.",
    },
  ],
  // The writer says everything in one message, the collaborator answers, and
  // the writer builds without replying. Silence accepts the details the
  // collaborator added (Pell, his theodolite, the strongbox) but not the
  // events it foretold, and nothing hidden may be shown.
  Unanswered: [
    {
      role: "user",
      content:
        "A ferrywoman, Brisa Calloway, works the Marrow crossing with her nephew Dov, who came to help for the season. The bridge commission has stopped paying the ferry's subsidy. Dov has already signed the ferry's landing rights over to the commission and hasn't told her. I want her to find out on her own.",
    },
    {
      role: "assistant",
      content:
        "Then a commission surveyor called Pell arrives with a brass theodolite while Dov is away upriver buying rope, and walks the landing as if it were his. Brisa goes to the tin strongbox under her bunk for the landing deed and finds it gone. Dov's signature is on the transfer.",
    },
  ],
  // The collaborator's reply contradicts two things the writer said, and adds
  // a person. The writer's version stands; the person may be kept.
  Contradicted: [
    {
      role: "user",
      content:
        "A clockmaker, Ansel Roe, keeps the tower clock in Verrin with his daughter Mab, who is twelve. The council has cut his stipend by half. I want Mab to end up keeping the clock herself.",
    },
    {
      role: "assistant",
      content:
        "Then Mab is nineteen and already does the winding, because Ansel's hands shake too badly to hold a file. The council's clerk, Orrin Slate, has noticed whose hands are on the weights, and the stipend was stopped altogether last spring.",
    },
  ],
};

// Each thing to come is matched as the event, never as a bare invented noun:
// the model is free to call the widow Quillane or to say a post at Orrowmere
// is on offer, since both are so when the story opens. What must not be shown
// is the fire, the Catalogue, or the leaving.
const FIRE = /Quillane Fire|burn\w*\b[^.\n]*\bdown\b/i;
const CATALOGUE = /Vessarine Catalogue/i;
const LEAVING = /\b(leav\w*|left|depart\w*)\b[^.\n]{0,20}\b(for|to)\s+Orrowmere/i;

// The Unanswered talk. What must never be shown is the hidden signing, in any
// of the words the talk used for it, and the events the collaborator foretold.
const SIGNED = /\bsign\w*|signature|landing rights/i;
const SECRET_SHOWN =
  /\bsign(ed|ing|s)?\b|signature|\btransfer\w*|\bdeed\b[^.\n|]*\b(gone|missing)\b/i;
const FORETOLD = /\barriv\w*|\b(finds?|found|learns?|discovers?)\b/i;
const FINDS_OUT = /\b(finds?|found|learns?|discovers?)\b/i;

// What this does not send that the shipped Build turn does: no Foundation or
// Setting, no [WORLD]/[THREADS] block (every fixture starts from an empty
// world), and no continuation. Its numbers describe a first Build on an empty
// story.
const messages = (talk) => [
  { role: "system", content: `${SCENARIO_BUILD_PROMPT}\n\n${REGISTER}` },
  ...talk,
  { role: "user", content: SCENARIO_BUILD_INSTRUCTION },
  { role: "assistant", content: SCENARIO_BUILD_PREFILL },
];

// --- read:start ---
// Mirrors the five-segment THREAD regex in src/core/utils/crucible-command-parser.ts.
const THREAD = /^\[\s*THREAD\s+"([^"]+)"\s*\|([^|]+?)\|([^|]*?)\|([^|]*?)\|([^|\]]*?)\]?\s*$/;
const CREATE = /^\[\s*CREATE\s+([A-Z]+)\s+"([^"]+)"\s*\|\s*(.+?)\]?\s*$/;

// Everything the story model could be shown: every element's name and summary,
// and every Thread's title and state. A name or a title is shown as surely as a
// summary is. The two private segments are kept apart: `wishes` is where a
// thing to come belongs, and `privates` is where it must not be copied, because
// the private segment is written into entries as fact when a Thread concludes.
const read = (text) => {
  const shown = [];
  const wishes = [];
  const privates = [];
  const created = [];
  let threads = 0;
  for (const raw of text.split(/\r\n|\r|\n/)) {
    // [CREATE THREAD …] is read as a THREAD, as the product reads it.
    const line = raw.trim().replace(/^\[\s*CREATE\s+THREAD\b/i, "[THREAD");
    const t = THREAD.exec(line);
    if (t) {
      threads++;
      shown.push(t[1], t[3]);
      privates.push(t[4]);
      wishes.push(t[5]);
      continue;
    }
    const c = CREATE.exec(line);
    if (c) {
      shown.push(c[2], c[3]);
      created.push({ type: c[1], name: c[2] });
    }
  }
  return {
    shown: shown.join("\n"),
    wishes: wishes.join("\n"),
    privates: privates.join("\n"),
    threads,
    created,
  };
};
// --- read:end ---

// --- unasked:start ---
// People, places and factions the conversation never mentioned. A name counts
// as mentioned when the talk contains it whole, or any of its words of four
// letters or more. Situations, systems and topics are left out: the model coins their
// names, so a name the talk lacks says nothing.
const NAMED_TYPES = new Set(["CHARACTER", "LOCATION", "FACTION"]);
const unasked = (created, conversation) => {
  const talk = new Set(conversation.toLowerCase().split(/[^a-z]+/));
  const said = conversation.toLowerCase();
  return created.filter(
    (c) =>
      NAMED_TYPES.has(c.type) &&
      // A short name ("Dov", "Mab Roe") has no four-letter word to match on:
      // it is mentioned when the talk used it whole or used every word of it.
      !said.includes(c.name.toLowerCase()) &&
      !c.name
        .toLowerCase()
        .split(/[^a-z]+/)
        .filter(Boolean)
        .every((w) => talk.has(w)) &&
      !c.name
        .toLowerCase()
        .split(/[^a-z]+/)
        .some((w) => w.length >= 4 && talk.has(w)),
  ).length;
};
// --- unasked:end ---

// Each fixture states its contract in one sentence; `holds` is that sentence,
// checked against the already-read reply.
const FIXTURES = [
  {
    name: "ToCome",
    contract:
      "a thing to come is written in a wish and appears in nothing the story model is shown, nor in a private segment",
    talk: TALKS.ToCome,
    holds: (r) =>
      FIRE.test(r.wishes) && !FIRE.test(r.shown) && !FIRE.test(r.privates),
  },
  {
    name: "AlreadySo",
    contract:
      "a thing already so is written in what the story model is shown and in no wish",
    talk: TALKS.AlreadySo,
    holds: (r) => FIRE.test(r.shown) && !FIRE.test(r.wishes),
  },
  {
    name: "TwoWishes",
    contract:
      "two things to come are each written in a wish and neither appears in anything shown, nor in a private segment",
    talk: TALKS.TwoWishes,
    holds: (r) =>
      /Vessarine|publish/i.test(r.wishes) &&
      /Orrowmere/i.test(r.wishes) &&
      !CATALOGUE.test(r.shown) &&
      !LEAVING.test(r.shown) &&
      !CATALOGUE.test(r.privates) &&
      !LEAVING.test(r.privates),
  },
  {
    name: "Unanswered",
    contract:
      "a hidden thing is recorded in a private segment and in nothing shown, an event the collaborator foretold is shown nowhere, and the finding out is in a wish",
    talk: TALKS.Unanswered,
    parts: {
      "secret shown": (r) => SECRET_SHOWN.test(r.shown),
      "secret not in a private segment": (r) => !SIGNED.test(r.privates),
      "event to come shown": (r) => FORETOLD.test(r.shown),
      "finding out not in a wish": (r) => !FINDS_OUT.test(r.wishes),
    },
    holds: (r) =>
      !SECRET_SHOWN.test(r.shown) &&
      SIGNED.test(r.privates) &&
      !FORETOLD.test(r.shown) &&
      FINDS_OUT.test(r.wishes),
  },
  {
    name: "Contradicted",
    contract:
      "where the collaborator contradicts the writer, the writer's version is recorded and the collaborator's is not",
    talk: TALKS.Contradicted,
    parts: {
      "collaborator's version recorded": (r) =>
        /nineteen|stopped altogether/i.test(`${r.shown}\n${r.privates}`),
      "writer's version dropped": (r) =>
        !/twelve/i.test(r.shown) || !/\bhalf\b|halved/i.test(r.shown),
    },
    holds: (r) =>
      !/nineteen|stopped altogether/i.test(`${r.shown}\n${r.privates}`) &&
      /twelve/i.test(r.shown) &&
      /\bhalf\b|halved/i.test(r.shown),
  },
];

let report = "";

function log(line) {
  report += line + "\n";
  api.v1.log(line);
  void api.v1.ui.updateParts([{ id: "report", text: report }]);
}

async function runFixture(fixture) {
  let failing = 0;
  let unparsed = 0;
  let threw = 0;
  let built = 0;
  let extra = 0;
  let worst = 0;
  // A fixture may name the separate ways it can fail; each is counted.
  const parts = Object.entries(fixture.parts ?? {});
  const partCounts = parts.map(() => 0);
  const talkText = fixture.talk.map((m) => m.content).join("\n");
  let firstFailure = "";
  let firstError = "";
  for (let run = 0; run < RUNS; run++) {
    let text;
    try {
      if (api.v1.script.getAllowedOutput() < PARAMS.max_tokens) {
        log(
          `  ${fixture.name} run ${run + 1}: waiting for output budget — press Continue`,
        );
      }
      await api.v1.script.waitForAllowedOutput(PARAMS.max_tokens);
      // One at a time: concurrent script generations are refused.
      const response = await api.v1.generate(messages(fixture.talk), PARAMS);
      text = `${SCENARIO_BUILD_PREFILL}${response.choices?.[0]?.text ?? ""}`;
    } catch (e) {
      threw++;
      if (!firstError) firstError = `${e?.message ?? e}`;
      continue;
    }
    const r = read(text);
    const failed = r.threads === 0 || !fixture.holds(r);
    if (r.threads === 0) unparsed++;
    const why = [];
    parts.forEach(([name, test], i) => {
      if (!test(r)) return;
      partCounts[i]++;
      why.push(name);
    });
    if (failed) {
      failing++;
      // Shown at once, not at the end: twenty runs is a long wait to learn
      // what a failing reply looked like.
      if (!firstFailure) {
        firstFailure = text;
        log(`  first failing output:\n${text}`);
      }
    }
    const n = unasked(r.created, talkText);
    built += r.created.length;
    extra += n;
    worst = Math.max(worst, n);
    log(
      `  ${fixture.name} run ${run + 1}: ${failed ? "FAIL" : "pass"}, ${n} unasked${why.length ? ` (${why.join("; ")})` : ""}`,
    );
  }
  const measured = RUNS - threw;
  const per = (total) => (measured > 0 ? (total / measured).toFixed(1) : "0.0");
  log(
    `${fixture.name}: ${failing} failing runs of ${measured} measured (${unparsed} with no THREAD parsed, ${threw} not measured) — ${fixture.contract} — built ${per(built)} per run, ${per(extra)} unasked (worst ${worst})`,
  );
  parts.forEach(([name], i) =>
    log(`  ${name}: ${partCounts[i]} runs of ${measured} measured`),
  );
  if (firstError) log(`  first run not measured: ${firstError}`);
}

async function run(fixtures) {
  report = "";
  log(`Scenario probe — ${RUNS} runs per fixture on ${MODEL}`);
  for (const fixture of fixtures) await runFixture(fixture);
  log("done");
}

api.v1.ui.register([
  api.v1.ui.extension.scriptPanel({
    name: "Scenario Probe",
    content: [
      api.v1.ui.part.column({
        content: [
          api.v1.ui.part.button({
            text: "Run all",
            callback: () => run(FIXTURES),
            disabledWhileCallbackRunning: true,
          }),
          // One fixture at a time: twenty runs is a quarter of an hour.
          ...FIXTURES.map((fixture) =>
            api.v1.ui.part.button({
              text: `Run ${fixture.name}`,
              callback: () => run([fixture]),
              disabledWhileCallbackRunning: true,
            }),
          ),
          // Does nothing itself: a budget wait only ends once a real button
          // has been pressed, and Run is disabled while the probe is running.
          api.v1.ui.part.button({
            text: "Continue (press when waiting for budget)",
            callback: () => {},
          }),
          api.v1.ui.part.text({
            id: "report",
            text: "Press a Run button. Report each line as N failing runs of M measured.",
            noTemplate: true,
            style: { whiteSpace: "pre-wrap", userSelect: "text" },
          }),
        ],
      }),
    ],
  }),
]);
